State per loop index: `{ warned: false }`, used only to warn once about a non-finite side. Values are stateless.

Each frame, per loop index:
```
const finite = (n: number): number => {
  if (Number.isFinite(n)) return n;
  if (!ctx.state.warned) {
    ctx.state.warned = true;
    ctx.services.log('warn', `${ctx.id}: a side isn't a finite number, so Edges uses 0 for it`);
  }
  return 0;
